updates: the 40 above, and 19 that end beyond the replay's copy of the
buffer, which is one to six units shorter than the buffer the editor had
written, and not beyond the editor's.

On devices. On an API 31 emulator with Gboard 10.8 and WebView 134, a
word was typed, the screen turned to landscape and back, and one letter
typed about eight seconds later. Without this patch 21 of 30 runs ended
damaged, 20 of them with the word doubled, on the disk too. With the
nine rules built, 100 of 101 runs were right: 39 of 40 on a new line and
40 of 40 on a line reached by a tap, both under a load held on the host,
and 21 of 21 on a quiet host, where the keyboard had the word open at
the letter in 20. The ninth rule's shape came in 31 of those runs and
was refused in each. The run that was not right ended line twx, the
letter over the last letter, as said above.

The write beyond the buffer was dispatched into the live editor through
the page, after the turn and with the keyboard attached: twox over one
unit that lies 65 units past the caret, as recorded, and x over a range
that starts before the caret and ends 20 units past the buffer, each
with a composition open that had typed nothing, with one that had typed,
and with none open. On a build with the nine rules and without the
refusal the lines after the caret were deleted on the disk in 12 runs of
